es also problematic. A's not open to new ideas could affect adaptability.\n\nMaybe B is still best because reliability and stress are top, and we could address communication issues with training. But nasty remarks are serious. Could be disqualifying. D's hot temper also serious. C's egocentric and communication issues also serious. A's show-off and not open to new ideas also serious.\n\nWe need to pick one. I think B's conscientiousness and stress handling are key for safety. Nasty remarks could be mitigated. So I will recommend Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion (none) but we can say \"Given we have not yet discussed, I propose...\". Provide evidence: very conscientious, handles stress well, but note concern about nasty remarks. Explain why still choose B.\n\nLet's produce public message and metadata."}
